From b094dbc7059137aec8dcf19cd4c0ff9d59da4f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:58:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] drm: apple: Route the J613 left-front display where the
 compositor pairs it

With the lid closed the panel's connector reads disconnected, so the
internal pipe's CRTC is free, and aquamarine (Hyprland) gives a display
that comes up on the left-front port the lowest free CRTC it can use:
the internal pipe's, index 0, below dcpext's. The fabric ranked the
internal pipe after dcpext, as a hybrid, so it routed that display to
dcpext: every mode then failed the atomic check, and when the lid
opened the panel found its only CRTC taken and stayed dark.

Rank the internal pipe as a plain pipeline while it is free (lid
closed, panel and its CRTC off), i.e. before dcpext, as the compositor
pairs. dcpext still keeps a display it already drives, and a display
arriving on the left-back port while dcpext drives the left-front one
still moves that one to the internal pipe; the move now shares its code
(dcp_typec_clamshell_move()) with the case below.

Boot with the lid closed: a panel CRTC that was never switched on counts
as blank, so the pipe is free as soon as the lid is reported closed, and
before a compositor owns the displays a left-front display that took
dcpext first moves to the internal pipe (dcp_typec_clamshell_settle()).

Lid open: a left-front display that leaves the internal pipe for a free
dcpext reads disconnected until the panel's connector is connected
again (at most 3 s), and is reported 200 ms after it, so that the
compositor gives the panel its CRTC back and the display dcpext's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017YMqWu7A3VwEYtHaA1TusK
